{%- comment -%}
  The free delivery threshold, formatted, from the one setting that defines it.

  Every "free delivery over X" line on the site renders this, so the number can
  only ever be changed in one place: Brand > Free delivery threshold.

  The parsing and the cents live in free-delivery-cents, which the cart page and
  the bag drawer also render — this snippet only formats. It deliberately does no
  arithmetic of its own: it used to repeat `times: 100`, and when the threshold
  gained decimals that became a second place to get the rounding right.

  money vs money_without_trailing_zeros is decided on the cents, not left to the
  filter. A whole-euro threshold reads "€60" rather than "€60.00", and a decimal
  one reads "€54.99" rather than being rounded to "€55" — which is what the site
  showed for as long as the setting was a `number`.

  Usage: {% render 'free-delivery-amount' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture fd_cents -%}{%- render 'free-delivery-cents' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign fd_c = fd_cents | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign fd_rem = fd_c | modulo: 100 -%}
{%- if fd_rem == 0 -%}{{- fd_c | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}{%- else -%}{{- fd_c | money -}}{%- endif -%}
